{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00968",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 1.85,
      "end_seconds": 12.53,
      "duration_seconds": 10.68,
      "text": "Dr Whitaker, here's Mr Lindqvist. Obs done: blood pressure 152 over 94, pulse 72. He's here about his results."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 14.24,
      "end_seconds": 23.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.93,
      "text": "Thank you, nurse. Mr Lindqvist, come in. Tell me what you understand about why you're here. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 25.76,
      "end_seconds": 38.05,
      "duration_seconds": 12.29,
      "text": "Er, the letter said something about protein in my water, and that my pressure was up. That's about all I've got, I'm afraid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 39.58,
      "end_seconds": 49.49,
      "duration_seconds": 9.91,
      "text": "That's fine, that's what I wanted to explain. Have you noticed anything yourself in the toilet?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 51.38,
      "end_seconds": 65.08,
      "duration_seconds": 13.7,
      "text": "It's, er, a bit frothy. Foamy. I noticed it a while back, I don't know, a few months? Maybe more. I can't pin it down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 68.16,
      "end_seconds": 74.36,
      "duration_seconds": 6.2,
      "text": "Foamy urine, a few months or more. Thank you. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.3,
      "end_seconds": 80.32,
      "duration_seconds": 3.02,
      "text": "Is that important? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 82.03,
      "end_seconds": 90.72,
      "duration_seconds": 8.69,
      "text": "It can be, because foam sometimes means protein is leaking through the kidneys. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.06,
      "end_seconds": 94.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.56,
      "text": "Leaking? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 97.28,
      "end_seconds": 111.17,
      "duration_seconds": 13.89,
      "text": "Think of the kidneys as a very fine sieve. Normally it keeps protein in the blood. When the sieve is under strain, some gets through. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.53,
      "end_seconds": 118.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.59,
      "text": "And the blood pressure causes that? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 119.81,
      "end_seconds": 130.43,
      "duration_seconds": 10.62,
      "text": "High blood pressure can strain the sieve, and kidney trouble can also push the blood pressure up. They feed each other. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 132.72,
      "end_seconds": 135.75,
      "duration_seconds": 3.03,
      "text": "A vicious circle. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 137.64,
      "end_seconds": 143.24,
      "duration_seconds": 5.6,
      "text": "Exactly. Any operations in the past that I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 146.58,
      "end_seconds": 150.19,
      "duration_seconds": 3.61,
      "text": "My appendix, in 1999. That's all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 153.51,
      "end_seconds": 159.08,
      "duration_seconds": 5.57,
      "text": "Right. Nurse, can you pop him on the couch? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 171.71,
      "end_seconds": 173.36,
      "duration_seconds": 1.65,
      "text": "Of course."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 175.78,
      "end_seconds": 183.73,
      "duration_seconds": 7.95,
      "text": "Your ankles, Mr Lindqvist, let me press. There's no swelling in either ankle."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 187.02,
      "end_seconds": 188.5,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Good. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 190.77,
      "end_seconds": 205.08,
      "duration_seconds": 14.31,
      "text": "Let me explain what I'd like to do. The first thing is to repeat the urine test, with a proper measurement of the protein."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.03,
      "end_seconds": 208.61,
      "duration_seconds": 1.58,
      "text": "Okay. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 211.99,
      "end_seconds": 219.18,
      "duration_seconds": 7.19,
      "text": "I'd also like to arrange blood tests to check how well your kidneys are working."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 222.11,
      "end_seconds": 225.23,
      "duration_seconds": 3.12,
      "text": "Is it serious? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 227.79,
      "end_seconds": 234.87,
      "duration_seconds": 7.08,
      "text": "It's too early to say. That's why we need the tests. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 236.78,
      "end_seconds": 240.84,
      "duration_seconds": 4.06,
      "text": "I understand. How long will it take? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 242.31,
      "end_seconds": 253.85,
      "duration_seconds": 11.54,
      "text": "A week or so for the results. The nurse will give you a pot for the urine sample. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 257.12,
      "end_seconds": 263.96,
      "duration_seconds": 6.84,
      "text": "I've got it here, Mr Lindqvist. First thing in the morning, please. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 265.74,
      "end_seconds": 270.25,
      "duration_seconds": 4.51,
      "text": "First thing in the morning, got it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 271.92,
      "end_seconds": 278.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.99,
      "text": "Keep your salt low, and don't take anti-inflammatory painkillers like ibuprofen for now."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 281.58,
      "end_seconds": 284.35,
      "duration_seconds": 2.77,
      "text": "Right, I'll remember. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 287.63,
      "end_seconds": 300.01,
      "duration_seconds": 12.38,
      "text": "If the protein is still there on the repeat, I'd like to see you again and talk about a referral to a kidney specialist."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 302.94,
      "end_seconds": 306.0,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Understood. Thank you, doctor. ~"
    }
  ]
}
